Sval: Remove address and card autofill

Firefox's address and card autofill is locked off (Sval spec §7.3), so
its built-in add-on registered actors and settings that never ran. The
component goes with what only it used: the native card field model and
its ChromeUtils entry, the FormHandler actor, the save prompts, the
settings groups and their dialogs, the addresses and credit cards sync
engines, the import of payment methods from Chrome, the policies,
prefs, Nimbus features, targeting attributes, strings and tests. Form
history, which still refuses to keep a card number, and the DOM's
autocomplete and autofill states stay.

